# Configure with locally generated synthetic demo values only.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/ttworkshop
# Must be the dedicated local test database; integration tests truncate its tables.
PG_TEST_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/ttworkshop_test
APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
PORT=3000
NODE_ENV=development
# For Cloud Run: APP_HOST=0.0.0.0, SERVE_WEB=true, PORT=8080,
# NODE_ENV=production, APP_ORIGIN=https://<actual-cloud-run-origin>.
# DATABASE_URL must be injected from Secret Manager; never commit its real value.
# Production API startup performs a read-only schema check; migrations must run
# in a separately authorized migration job with a different DB user/SA/Secret.
# Local defaults stay unchanged to preserve Docker Compose and Vite development.
# APP_HOST=0.0.0.0
# SERVE_WEB=true
# To seed local synthetic identities, provide SEED_PASSWORD in your shell.
# Never commit a real credential or a .env with secrets.
# University timezone for datetime display (IANA format)
VITE_UNIVERSITY_TIMEZONE=Asia/Bangkok
# Dedicated database for the seed idempotency suite (R-11 test isolation).
# Created and migrated automatically by tests/seedIdempotency.test.ts.
# Must be a DIFFERENT database from PG_TEST_URL so seed runs can never
# overwrite credentials or truncate rows used by the other suites.
PG_SEED_TEST_URL=postgresql://localhost:5432/ttworkshop_seed_test
